Hi,

> But in debian sarge I found three Qt3-dev packages.

the correct one is libqt3-mt-dev.

However, the easiest way to install all build dependencies (and the 
dependencies those have in turn) on a debian based system is:

# apt-get build-dep rkward

For completeness, though:

> 	kde-devel (and kde-devel-extras?)

kdelibs4-dev

> 	php4-dev

No, you just need php4-cli (or php5-cli), no -dev needed in this case.

> 	build-essential (in Sarge, I can't find build-dep)

Yes, you'll need that.

> But I can't find the r-cran-dev or the R-headers in debian sarge.

r-base-dev

Regards
Thomas
